A||||5||jch82||Third Brake Light Install??||||5||
Z||000000||jch82||08-18-2001||04:04 PM||||I just got a third brake light setup for my 85gt (not equipped with one). What do I need for the install and where do I run the wires??? I know a little bit about electrical work, but I guess not enough...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Thanks!<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||08-18-2001||04:24 PM||||I would reccomend taping into the brake switch at the pedal.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Joe Torma||08-18-2001||05:34 PM||||There is a wire in the long flat connector by the brake pedal area, on the steering column...I'm pretty sure it's white, use that one.  Take a meter or test light to it and hit the brake pedal see if you get juice.<P>It should be there on your GT...I used to use this when I used to wire up Countachs with non GT wiring harnesses(seperate turn signals).||||reg||1
Z||000003||jch82||08-20-2001||01:36 PM||||Is it one of these plugs??<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/thirdbrakelight.jpg"> <P>Thanks<P><BR>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000004||theogre||08-20-2001||08:01 PM||||Unless that pic is reversed,,,  I think those are on the clutch. you want the brake for a light...<P>The switch with the big yellow and purple wires is the starter interlock. the other one I think it the cruise release.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 08-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Tigger||08-20-2001||11:15 PM||||Yes, its the switch on the brake pedal.  There is a black plug with orange and white wires.  The wire for the third brake light goes to the white wire on my Fiero.  For mine I put the wire in the plug then snapped it on so there is no soldering or wire ties.  I might be wrong but I think that's the only wire you have to worry about, I think the ground is direct to the frame.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 08-20-2001).]||||reg||1
